# R23 Volunteers (side quest): Tamsin Ledger's militia roll. By hand, polished by Gemini, unvoiced.

~ start
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: Unless this militia is enrolled in triplicate, it is merely a riot with pitchforks. I require three signatures on the muster roll. Sergeant Gaunt, Mr Quill, and Mr Pennywhistle promised to sign, though each has lodged a formal grievance.
give wv_signed_roll
set wv_vol_asked
quest vigil_volunteers asked
-> menu

~ menu
* Ask what their grievances are -> objections
* Ask what separates a lawful militia from a mob -> lawful
* Take the muster roll and go -> END

~ objections
tamsin_ledger [weary]: Sergeant Gaunt demands the rear guard. Mr Quill insists his elegy be adopted as our regimental hymn. Mr Pennywhistle wants it recorded that he is an independent contractor, not a volunteer. I have initialled all three.
-> menu

~ lawful
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: A lawful militia may be commanded to hold a line. A mob may only be implored. In practice it is the exact same neighbours, only with better bookkeeping.
-> menu

~ progress
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: Three signatures are required for the quorum. I am keeping tally in the margin.
-> progress_menu

~ progress_menu
* [if flag.vol_signed >= 3] Present the completed muster roll -> file
* Ask whose signatures are still missing -> missing
* [if item:wv_last_letters and not flag.letter_tamsin] Deliver the letter from the county seat -> vigil/letters:to_tamsin
* [ends:vigil_volunteers] Tell her the roll will go unsigned -> refuse
* Leave her to her ledgers -> END

~ missing
if not flag.vol_gaunt
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: Sergeant Gaunt has yet to sign. He is down by the barricade, inspecting the rear.
endif
if not flag.vol_quill
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: Mr Quill is still missing. He is in the inn yard, wrestling with a stanza.
endif
if not flag.vol_barnaby
tamsin_ledger [neutral]: Mr Pennywhistle has not signed. He has set up shop beside the notice board.
endif
if flag.vol_signed >= 3
tamsin_ledger [smile]: That is all three names accounted for. Hand me the roll.
endif
-> progress_menu

~ file
tamsin_ledger [smile]: In triplicate, witnessed, stamped, and entered into the parish archive. Wickermoor now possesses a properly constituted militia. It is remarkable how much steadier one's hands feel once the ink is dry.
take wv_signed_roll
quest vigil_volunteers filed
set vol_resolved
set wv_militia_lawful
temp_hp 2d8 party
-> END

~ refuse
tamsin_ledger [sad]: A mob it shall be, then. I will rule a diagonal line through the page. The barricade will simply have to be held by whoever happens to be standing behind it.
take wv_signed_roll
quest vigil_volunteers refused
set vol_resolved
-> END

~ after
if flag.wv_militia_lawful
tamsin_ledger [smile]: Our company is duly registered. Should the Wicker Man breach the square, it will be trespassing against an incorporated body.
else
tamsin_ledger [weary]: Whoever stands at the planks tonight does so in an unofficial capacity. I have logged the irregularity.
endif
-> END

~ desk
Narrator: A trestle table smells of iron gall ink and damp wool. The queue of villagers loops round the well and back again, because Tamsin requires every soul to sign two separate ledgers.
-> END

~ gaunt
sgt_gaunt [smile]: Sign the clerk's parchment? With pleasure, once my post is settled. I am volunteering for the rear. Vital ground, the rear. I have never lost an engagement I survived the end of, and I see no reason to break the streak.
-> gaunt_menu

~ gaunt_menu
* [Persuasion DC 13] Assure him the rear guard needs his signature first -> gaunt_sign | gaunt_stall
* [Intimidation DC 13] Remind him the Wicker Man can step over the front -> gaunt_sign | gaunt_stall
* Offer to write him in as Commander of the Rear -> gaunt_rear
* Leave him to his post -> END

~ gaunt_sign
Narrator: He signs with a sweeping loop of the quill, the florid mark of a man endorsing a promissory note he never intends to honour.
set vol_gaunt
set vol_signed += 1
-> END

~ gaunt_stall
sgt_gaunt [sad]: I would put my name down this instant, truly, but the nib has split. Best wait until the wind drops.
-> gaunt_menu

~ gaunt_rear
Narrator: He puffs out his breastplate, prints REAR GUARD across the vellum in block capitals twice the height of his name, and signs beneath it.
set vol_gaunt
set vol_signed += 1
-> END
